From c1fbb2b6f16b1f0089b9625e1ba11830f4c4d685 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 23:45:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] fix: report landing sign-in failures and give primary
 buttons a visible fill

Observed on the deployed preview (7b240f7): clicking 'Sign in securely'
did nothing. startLogin() rejects when OIDC is not configured or
/api/oauth/begin fails, and the landing onClick dropped the rejection,
so users got no feedback. The button also rendered transparent because
the shadcn bg-primary utility had no --color-primary theme token.

- Catch startLogin() on the landing CTA and show a role=alert message.
- Define --color-primary / --color-primary-foreground from the existing
  --deep palette token.
- E2E regression: forced /api/oauth/begin 503 must surface an alert and
  the CTA must have a non-transparent background (fails before the fix).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ADMGPDEiCj5xPwmjpf1nob
